+<section class="section" id="techniques" aria-labelledby="techniques-heading">
+  <div class="container">
+
+    <div class="section-eyebrow">
+      <span class="tag">// how it actually works</span>
+    </div>
+    <h2 id="techniques-heading" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem;">
+      Core AIOps <span class="text-green">Techniques</span>
+    </h2>
+    <p style="max-width:640px; margin-bottom:2rem;">
+      Most AIOps value comes from a handful of techniques, and many work with the
+      Prometheus and Alertmanager you already run, no ML platform required.
+    </p>
+
+    <div class="tech-grid">
+      <div class="tech-card">
+        <h3>📉 Dynamic baselines (z-score)</h3>
+        <p>Instead of a fixed threshold, compare a metric to its own recent history. A z-score above 3 means "much higher than usual for this service".</p>
+        <div class="guide-code"><span class="c"># how unusual is the current request rate?</span>
+(
+  rate(http_requests_total[5m])
+  - avg_over_time(rate(http_requests_total[5m])[1d:5m])
+)
+/ stddev_over_time(rate(http_requests_total[5m])[1d:5m])</div>
+      </div>
+      <div class="tech-card">
+        <h3>📅 Seasonality</h3>
+        <p>Traffic at 9am Monday looks nothing like 3am Sunday. Compare against the same time last week to cut false alarms on predictable peaks.</p>
+        <div class="guide-code"><span class="c"># current traffic vs the same time 1 week ago</span>
+sum(rate(http_requests_total[5m]))
+/
+sum(rate(http_requests_total[5m] offset 1w))</div>
+      </div>
+      <div class="tech-card">
+        <h3>🔮 Forecasting</h3>
+        <p>Predict problems before they happen. A linear forecast catches a disk that will fill up hours before any threshold alert would fire.</p>
+        <div class="guide-code"><span class="c"># disk predicted to run out within 4 hours</span>
+predict_linear(
+  node_filesystem_avail_bytes{fstype!="tmpfs"}[6h],
+  4 * 3600
+) &lt; 0</div>
+      </div>
+      <div class="tech-card">
+        <h3>🧩 Alert correlation &amp; noise reduction</h3>
+        <p>One failing database can trigger fifty alerts. Group related alerts into one notification, and suppress symptoms when the cause is already firing.</p>
+        <div class="guide-code"><span class="c"># alertmanager.yml</span>
+route:
