+    <h2 id="lab-heading" style="margin-bottom:0.5rem;">
+      Build Your Own <span class="text-green">AIOps Lab</span>
+    </h2>
+    <p style="max-width:640px; margin-bottom:2rem;">
+      Six steps from an empty laptop to an AI agent that triages real alerts on a local Kubernetes cluster.
+      Everything runs locally except the LLM API calls.
+    </p>
+
+    <div class="lab-steps">
+      <div class="lab-step">
+        <h3>Create a cluster with observability</h3>
+        <p>Start a <code>kind</code> cluster, install <code>kube-prometheus-stack</code> and Loki, and deploy a sample app. Projects <a href="projects.html#k8s-helm">05</a> and <a href="projects.html#observability">06</a> walk through this.</p>
+        <div class="guide-code">kind create cluster --name aiops
+helm upgrade --install monitoring prometheus-community/kube-prometheus-stack \
+  -n monitoring --create-namespace</div>
+      </div>
+
+      <div class="lab-step">
+        <h3>Give the agent a read-only identity</h3>
+        <p>The agent's service account can read pods, logs, events and deployments, and nothing else: no writes, and no Secrets.</p>
+        <div class="guide-code">apiVersion: rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1
+kind: ClusterRole
+metadata:
+  name: aiops-readonly
+rules:
+  - apiGroups: [""]
+    resources: ["pods", "pods/log", "events", "services", "nodes"]
+    verbs: ["get", "list", "watch"]
+  - apiGroups: ["apps"]
+    resources: ["deployments", "replicasets"]
+    verbs: ["get", "list", "watch"]</div>
+      </div>
+
+      <div class="lab-step">
+        <h3>Write the triage agent</h3>
+        <p>A short Python program gives an LLM three read-only tools (PromQL queries, events, pod logs) and asks it for a structured report: summary, evidence, likely cause, next steps and confidence.</p>
+        <p>Full, tested code: <a href="blog-llm-triage-agent.html">Build a Read-Only LLM Triage Agent for Kubernetes →</a></p>
+      </div>
+
+      <div class="lab-step">
+        <h3>Send alerts to the agent</h3>
+        <p>Route paging alerts to the agent through an Alertmanager webhook, and post its report to Slack or the incident channel. <code>continue: true</code> keeps your normal notifications working too.</p>
+        <div class="guide-code">route:
+  receiver: default
+  routes:
+    - matchers: [severity="page"]
+      receiver: aiops-agent
+      continue: true
+receivers:
+  - name: aiops-agent
+    webhook_configs:
+      - url: http://aiops-agent.aiops.svc:8080/alert</div>
+      </div>
+
+      <div class="lab-step">
+        <h3>Break things on purpose</h3>
+        <p>Inject the five faults above and grade each report: did the agent find the real cause? Did it admit when it wasn't sure? Keep a simple scorecard.</p>
